%% W1D3 — Naive vs. Agentic RAG — Request Flow
%% Shows the iterative retrieval loop, validation branches, and reformulation retry path
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant App as Application
    participant Classifier as Query Classifier
    participant Decomposer as Query Decomposer
    participant Retriever as Vector Store
    participant Validator as Evidence Validator
    participant LLM as LLM (Synthesis)

    User->>App: Submit multi-hop query
    App->>Classifier: Classify query type
    Classifier-->>App: multi-hop — route to agentic pipeline

    App->>Decomposer: Decompose query into sub-questions
    Decomposer->>LLM: Decomposition prompt
    LLM-->>Decomposer: ["sub-question 1", "sub-question 2"]
    Decomposer-->>App: Sub-question list (deduplicated)

    loop For each sub-question
        App->>Retriever: retrieve(sub-question, top_k=5)
        Retriever-->>App: chunks with similarity scores

        App->>Validator: validate(chunks, sub-question)
        alt Similarity >= threshold AND semantic match
            Validator-->>App: evidence accepted (confidence: high)
        else Similarity < threshold OR semantic mismatch
            Validator-->>App: evidence rejected
            App->>Retriever: retrieve(reformulated sub-question)
            Retriever-->>App: new chunks
            alt Reformulation succeeds
                Validator-->>App: evidence accepted (confidence: medium)
            else Max retries exceeded
                Validator-->>App: sub-question unanswerable
            end
        end
    end

    Note over App,LLM: Synthesis prompt includes all accepted evidence and any unanswerable flags
    App->>LLM: Synthesise answer from validated evidence
    LLM-->>App: Answer with inline citations
    App-->>User: Final response (partial if any sub-question unanswerable)
